RF.put("questb:b49",{"8689":{"id":8689,"t":"Shroud of Infinite Wisdom","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Martial Drape, 2 Jasper Idols, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Keyl Swiftclaw in Silithus. You must also obtain Revered reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Martial Drape General Rajaxx 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Kurinnaxx 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ayamiss the Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Buru the Gorger 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj\n2 Jasper Idol Flesh Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Gold Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Clay Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 21000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"I'm glad to hear you're aiding us in our attack on Ahn'Qiraj, ‹name›. I can make you a protective item that'll be of assistance in the fight against our enemy, ‹class›.\nI shall need a Qiraji drape, which I'll resize for you of course. I'll also need idols and scarabs which I'll use to create a suitable clasp.\nI promise you won't be disappointed.","rew":"You will receive:\nShroud of Infinite Wisdom\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring the materials for the cloak, ‹name›?","done":"Ah yes... this drape is immaculate.\nTake this cloak, ‹name›. May it protect you from the foul magic of the Qiraji.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.8,"y":39.5,"n":"Keyl Swiftclaw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8849":{"id":8849,"t":"Twenty Signets for War Supplies","lv":49,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"20 Alliance Commendation Signet","rew":"You will receive:\nAhn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.5,"y":34.7,"n":"Field Marshal Snowfall","s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8529":{"id":8529,"t":"The Alliance Needs More Spotted Yellowtail!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 spotted yellowtail to Huntress Swiftriver at the airfield in Dun Morogh.\n20 Spotted Yellowtail Raene Wolfrunner 0.7 % , Volcor 0.7 % , Terenthis 0.7 % , Sentinel Selarin 0.7 % and 4 more","desc":"If you're still willing I'd like to send you back out to bring in another haul of spotted yellowtail, ‹name›. I'd imagine with the expertise you gained the first time out that this catch should be much faster and easier. Are you game?","rew":"You will receive:\n7 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"If you're still willing I'd like to send you back out to bring in another haul of spotted yellowtail, ‹name›. I'd imagine with the expertise you gained the first time out that this catch should be much faster and easier. Are you game?","done":"You are a true member of the Alliance, ‹name›. Your efforts shall not go unnoticed, or unappreciated. And thank you for cooking up the fish as well. I will see to it that they are stored away properly, and then I'll need to update my count. Every one brings us that much closer to catching our goal.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.6,"y":32.2,"n":"Huntress Swiftriver","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8609":{"id":8609,"t":"The Horde Needs Runecloth Bandages!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 59.","obj":"Bring 20 Runecloth Bandages to Stoneguard Clayhoof at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n20 Runecloth Bandage","desc":"It appears inevitable that the Horde and Alliance are on a collision course for war at Ahn'Qiraj. Surprisingly, it is not a war with each other, but rather with the silithid, and whatever force controls them. Also surprisingly, both sides are doing their part to gather the resources necessary to wage a successful war.\nI am collecting runecloth bandages to distribute to the soldiers, but I won't be successful without assistance, hopefully yours. Is this something that you can aid me with, ‹class›?","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"Did you get the venom?","done":"Sweet, you got it!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.6,"y":75.8,"n":"Stoneguard Clayhoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"7169":{"id":7169,"t":"Honored Amongst the Guard","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Stormpike Insignia Rank 2","desc":"The base buzzes with news of your exploits in the Field of Strife! You have struck mighty blows against our enemy - crushing their morale! For this, you have earned a rank of honor among the Stormpike.\nPresent your insignia.","rew":"You will receive:\nStormpike Insignia Rank 3\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Stormpike Guard\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"The base buzzes with news of your exploits in the Field of Strife! You have struck mighty blows against our enemy - crushing their morale! For this, you have earned a rank of honor among the Stormpike.\nPresent your insignia.","done":"The king has been made aware of your battlefront heroics, ‹class›. Continue in your stalwart defense of the Stormpike Guard!","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":39.5,"y":81.2,"n":"Lieutenant Haggerdin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"8369":{"id":8369,"t":"Invaders of Alterac Valley","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Alterac Valley Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Alterac Valley Mark of Honor","desc":"Listen up, ‹name›. No matter what you might have heard about the battle raging in Alterac Valley, one thing remains true: the Stormpike Expedition invaded Frostwolf Territory. The day we allow the Alliance to invade Horde lands without a forceful response is the day I hang up my axe and live the rest of my life in shame. Go forth and expel the invaders!","rew":"Money: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 8,300\n+150 reputation with Frostwolf Clan","back":"What news do you bring from the lands of the Frostwolves? How does the battle for Alterac Valley fare?","done":"You've shown great bravery in protecting our lands in Alterac Valley! I will tell my superiors of your deeds.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"1009":{"id":1009,"t":"Ruuzel","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 2,550 experience instead of 2,250, 1.13 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Ring of Zoram to Talen near the Zoram Strand.\nRing of Zoram Ruuzel , Lady Vespia","desc":"I fear the ancient statuette's secrets will remain forever hidden unless you find the key to its ancient lock.\nThat key is a ring, the Ring of Zoram. It belonged to the rulers of this city before the waves of the Sundering drowned it.\nFor years the ring was lost, but the naga have recently found it.\nTheir leader, Ruuzel, dwells on an isle on the northern edge of Zoram. Please, ‹name›, retrieve the ring for me!","rew":"You will receive:\nRobes of Antiquity\nExperience: 2,550\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"It is said that the Ring of Zoram is the key to any lock within the city. Do you have it, ‹name›?","done":"You found the ring! Thank you, ‹name›. Please take this as payment, and know that your deeds today will remain forever in my memory.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":14.8,"y":31.3,"n":"Talen","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"5089":{"id":5089,"t":"General Drakkisath's Command","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 6,850, 0.96 times as much.","obj":"Take General Drakkisath's Command to Marshal Maxwell in Burning Steppes.\nGeneral Drakkisath's Command Overlord Wyrmthalak\nProvided: General Drakkisath's Command","desc":"From the corpse of the defeated serpent you uncover what appears to be a note of some importance: A letter from his superior, General Drakkisath, concerning protocol.\nYour instinct tells you that you should take it to Marshal Maxwell.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"What have you got there, ‹name›?","done":"The plot thickens...","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":84.7,"y":69,"n":"Marshal Maxwell","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"4769":{"id":4769,"t":"Vivian Lagrave and the Darkstone Tablet","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Shadowmage Vivian Lagrave.","desc":"Vivian Lagrave sent me word from Kargath, in the Badlands. Through her studies, she believes there is an ancient text within Blackrock Spire that would benefit our research. To confirm this, she will need someone to extract the text from the spire. No easy task.\nIf interested, then speak with Vivian in Kargath.","rew":"Experience: 650\n+10 reputation with Undercity","done":"It is true. I believe there is a tablet held within Blackrock Spire, a tablet that contains old alchemical recipes. I am glad you are here, for I need help in retrieving the tablet.\nMake yourself comfortable, and I will explain further.\nUndercity Badlands","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":50.1,"y":68,"n":"Apothecary Zinge","s":1},{"z":"Badlands","x":2.9,"y":47.8,"n":"Shadowmage Vivian Lagrave","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"7649":{"id":7649,"t":"Enchanted Thorium Platemail: Volume I","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 50 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 6,500, 1.02 times as much.","obj":"Return the book to its rightful owners.\nEnchanted Thorium Platemail\nProvided: Enchanted Thorium Platemail","desc":"The tome carries the mark of the Athenaeum.","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Enchanted Thorium Breastplate\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Shen'dralar","back":"You have recovered a tome!","done":"Well done, my boy.\n<Lorekeeper Lydros tears out a page from the book.>\nI am sure you can make use of this recipe.\nStart an item: Enchanted Thorium Platemail End Lorekeeper Lydros Level 60 , requires level 50 Difficulty 50 56 58 Side Both factions Type Dungeon Profession Blacksmithing 300 Shareable No Quest ID 7649","cats":["blacksmithing"]},"97969":{"id":97969,"t":"Camping 101 leatherworking","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Indari Sunseam in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your leatherworking skill to 20","desc":"You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, ‹class›. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels.","back":"Yes, I can teach you.","done":"There you have it, your very own camp tent. Most folk don't care much for tents being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":41.6,"y":44.8,"n":"Raan Wildwind","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":44.6,"y":44.4,"n":"Indari Sunseam","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94289":{"id":94289,"t":"Craftsmans writ gyromatic micro adjuster","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Gyromatic Micro-Adjuster\nGyromatic Micro-Adjustor","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Gyromatic Micro-Adjuster, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Gyromatic Micro-Adjuster Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94289","cats":["crafting"]},"9249":{"id":9249,"t":"40 tickets schematic steam tonk controller","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"40 Darkmoon Faire Prize Ticket","rew":"You will receive:\nSchematic: Steam Tonk Controller\nLevel 60 , requires level 45 Difficulty 45 56 58 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 9249","cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"7889":{"id":7889,"t":"Coarse Weightstone","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Coarse Weightstone","rew":"You will receive:\nDarkmoon Faire Prize Ticket\n+100 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"It takes a lot of work to be the strongest woman alive! My weight set is getting too light and if I'm to stay fit then I'll need more weights!\nDo you think you could bring me some weight stones? If you do, then I'll give you a Darkmoon Faire ticket.","done":"Great! These will work great! They're not too heavy, but not too light either. They're perfect for building muscle mass!\nThanks much, ‹name›. Here's your Darkmoon Faire ticket!\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.6,"y":46.4,"n":"Kerri Hicks","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":40.5,"y":69.9,"n":"Kerri Hicks","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"7489":{"id":7489,"t":"Lethtendris's Web","lv":57,"min":54,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Lethtendris's Web to Talo Thornhoof at Camp Mojache in Feralas.\nLethtendris's Web Lethtendris","desc":"The blood elf Lethtendris has overstepped her bounds. So eager was she to gather magical power that she defied her brethren and created a device of insidious design, a web meant to siphon the tainted magical energies of Dire Maul. Even now she gathers those energies and plans to release them against her enemies.\nLethtendris must be stopped. Find her within the Warpwood Quarter of Dire Maul, defeat her and bring her web to me so that it might be returned to more clear-headed blood elves for study.","rew":"You will receive:\nLorespinner\nMoney: 1 70 1 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 7,550\n+150 reputation with Horde","back":"‹name›, do you have Lethtendris's Web?","done":"You have done well, ‹name›. This web holds within it vast stores of the magic of Dire Maul, and I fear what damage may be unleashed if those energies were harnessed by one so irresponsible as Lethtendris. I am saddened by her death, but I know that she could never part with her web while alive.\nThank you, ‹name›. I will send the web to students of magic more responsible than Lethtendris. They will be the new wardens of its power.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":76.2,"y":43.8,"n":"Talo Thornhoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dire-maul"]},"6129":{"id":6129,"t":"Curing the Sick","lv":14,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Curative Animal Salve on 10 Sickly Gazelles that are located throughout the northern part of the Barrens; doing so should cure them. Sickly Gazelles have been reported north of the east-west road that runs through the Crossroads.\nSickly Gazelle cured : 0/ 10\nProvided: Curative Animal Salve","desc":"I was able to make enough salve for ten doses of curing, ‹name›. While I work with local authorities to try and make some more salve, I'd like for you to help us get a head start. All around the northern Barrens are sickly gazelles; use the salve on them and cure their malaise.\nDendrite Starblaze in Moonglade will want to talk to you when you're done, I'm sure. Please extend our thanks to the Cenarion Circle there... and let me say thanks to you directly for the help you've given!","rew":"You will receive:\nVeildust Medicine Bag\nExperience: 750\n+75 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Have you completed what was asked of you by Tonga Runetotem at the Crossroads? Your work is not complete unless it is.","done":"You have done well in tending to the sickly gazelles of the Barrens; they are unwitting victims of a greater taint and corruption that is spreading all throughout the land. You ‹race› are most eager to understand the ways of Cenarius; you, like your elders in Thunder Bluff, are proving that the need for balance transcends artificial racial barriers.\n‹name›, you've proven your worth as an friend of nature and the Circle - take this as a symbol of such.\nThe Barrens Moonglade","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.3,"y":31.9,"n":"Tonga Runetotem","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.6,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"1169":{"id":1169,"t":"Identifying the Brood","lv":43,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Draz'Zilb in Brackenwall Village would like you to bring him 15 Searing Tongues and 15 Searing Hearts.\n15 Searing Tongue Searing Hatchling 25 % , Searing Whelp 25 %\n15 Searing Heart Searing Hatchling 25 % , Searing Whelp 25 %","desc":"Whilst that craven fool, Mok'Morokk, wallows in power and Tharg wrestles the demons of sorrow and vengeance and vies for leadership of the clan, I seem to be the only one concerned with identifying the source of aggression on our old home.\nWhy the puzzled stare, ‹name›? Expecting me to speak like an uncouth ruffian merely because I am an ogre?\nNow back to business, bring to me the hearts and tongues from the whelps and hatchlings. I shall trace the root of this evil...","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nScorched Cape Rustler Gloves\nExperience: 5,350","back":"With the hearts and tongues of scorched offspring of the black dragon army, I can decipher what wretched beast introduced her spawn into our home. Perhaps with a greater knowledge of our aggressors, we can seek to destroy them once and for all and reclaim Stonemaul Village from ruin.\nOf course, convincing Mok'Morokk to move his lethargic, fat mass out of this muck hole is going to be an epic quest in and of itself...","done":"'Twas a perilous affair, no doubt, collecting all of these hearts and tongues. I shall delve into the depths of the arcane to trace the origin of the black menace which has descended upon our former home.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":37.2,"y":33.1,"n":"Draz'Zilb","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"8929":{"id":8929,"t":"In Search of Anthion","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Extra-Dimensional Ghost Revealer at the entrance to Stratholme and speak with the ghost of Anthion Harmon.\nProvided: Extra-Dimensional Ghost Revealer","desc":"Well, nothing left for us to do but try out the goblin's invention. Word has it that Anthion was mowed down by the undead legions of Stratholme as he tried to enter its gates.\nTry using the device there and find out whatever Anthion knew.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","done":"Deliana had you contact me? I'll do my best to help you, but first I must ask a great favor of you.\nDun Morogh Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":26.1,"y":11.3,"n":"Anthion Harmon","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"95809":{"id":95809,"t":"Heartwoven","lv":31,"min":24,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Return to Caitlin Grassman in Menethil Harbor.\nProvided: Reed-woven Heart","desc":"I need a moment to rest before I find my own way out.\n<He pulls some reeds from his pack and quickly braids and bends them into a heart.>\nTake this, and bring it back to Caitlin. Let her know I'll be home soon! Now that we have a path cleared out thanks to you, I'll gather my bushels and follow your trail.\nThank you.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n4 Greater Healing Potion 4 Mana Potion\nYou will also receive:\nSwiftness Potion Satchel of Potions\nExperience: 6,150","back":"I'm more than worried about him!","done":"Goodness, that sounds terrible!\nBy the light, I'm grateful he's one of the survivors.\n<She holds the reed-woven heart to her own.>\nI'll start cooking a hearty meal for him. Thank you for bringing me this. I'd like you to have something as a token of our appreciation.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":11.8,"y":58.6,"n":"Caitlin Grassman","e":1}],"cats":["excavation-site-wetlands-dungeon"]},"5889":{"id":5889,"t":"Salve via Gathering","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"4 Fel Creep Sungrass 15 % , Mountain Silversage 15 % , Dreamfoil 15 % , Golden Sansam 15 % and 3 more","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Cenarion Plant Salve\nExperience: 4,200","back":"A Cenarion beacon allows a seasoned herbalist to spot insidious fel creep - a malfeasant product of Felwood's corruption. My work here has taught me the knowledge of purifying fel creep into a cleansing reagent... used in what we now refer to as Cenarion plant salve.\nWhen you gather herbs in Felwood, you should encounter the fel creep so long as you have the beacon. In exchange for what you bring to me, I will give you pre-made Cenarion plant salve.","done":"Excellent work ‹name› - every bit of this, once we purify it, will help us take back Felwood. Here, take some doses of Cenarion plant salve and head into the forest. The reclaiming of the land from the corruption waits for no ‹race›!","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":46.7,"y":83.1,"n":"Maybess Riverbreeze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"5249":{"id":5249,"t":"To Winterspring!","lv":56,"min":53,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Starfall Village in Winterspring and speak with Wynd Nightchaser.","desc":"In Winterspring, to the north of here, there are many ancient elven ruins. It's a harsh land, but it holds many secrets and places to explore.\nWith all my work to do here in Felwood, I have not had the opportunity to travel to Winterspring. But there's no reason why you shouldn't!\nWhile you're there, look for Wynd Nightchaser. He spends most of his time in Starfall Village and he knows a lot about the area.","rew":"Experience: 575\n+10 reputation with Darnassus","done":"A friend of Ivy Leafrunner? Nice to meet you, ‹name›.\nFelwood Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":51,"y":81.6,"n":"Ivy Leafrunner","s":1},{"z":"Winterspring","x":52,"y":30.4,"n":"Wynd Nightchaser","e":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4129":{"id":4129,"t":"The Knife Revealed","lv":44,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Discarded Knife to Quintis Jonespyre in Feathermoon Stronghold.\nDiscarded Knife\nProvided: Discarded Knife","desc":"The Stronghold's resident druid, Quintis Jonespyre, has some... unusual skills. One of them involves psychometry - the ability to reveal an item's history by touch. Don't ask me how he does it; I chalk it up to magic I do not and choose not to understand. I do know, however, two things: one, I've seen it work and two, the bum owes me.\nTake the knife up to Quint in his little tree-house here, and tell him for me that his Kalimdor Hold 'Em debt will be paid if he works his mojo on that knife.","rew":"Experience: 380","back":"Ginro sent you, eh?\nMy psychometric readings are fairly draining on the psyche... but so are my losses at Kalimdor Hold 'Em. They call me \"King of the Bad Beats\" here in the Stronghold. Unlucky at cards... lucky at mastering the secrets of nature, I guess.\nAnyway, of course I'll do it. This may be just the breakthrough we need to uncover Raschal's fate. If you would hand me the knife, we can get started.","done":"Thank you, ‹name›.\nWhile psychometry isn't an exact art by any stretch of the imagination, I've used it in times past to give insight into situations that others have chalked up to lost causes. I think using it on the knife you've uncovered will give us a glimpse into what happened to Raschal.\nIt will only take a moment to do, but it isn't what I'd call a caster-friendly task. Bear with me on this.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":31.9,"y":45.1,"n":"Ginro Hearthkindle","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":32.4,"y":43.8,"n":"Quintis Jonespyre","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"6609":{"id":6609,"t":"I Got Nothin' Left!","lv":45,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Kalimdor, to the coastal city of Theramore. From there you must search for an island, south of the main town. Nat Pagle awaits your arrival!","desc":"I'm a dwarf fer cryin' out loud, lad/missy! I ain't been designed to fish! I mean look at me! I'm practically made outta stone.\nI got nothin' left - ye tapped me out. I've taught ye all I know, flipflop!\nDon't ye get it? Ah, fine. I got an ol' friend over on Kalimdor who can help ye out. 'Is name be Nat Pagle, a fine lad. Find him on the islands south o' Theramore. Git goin'!","rew":"Experience: 975","done":"I've always got room on my island for visitors... I reckon...\nDun Morogh Dustwallow Marsh","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.8,"y":22.2,"n":"Grimnur Stonebrand","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":58.6,"y":60.1,"n":"Nat Pagle","e":1}],"cats":["fishing"]},"2929":{"id":2929,"t":"The Grand Betrayal","lv":35,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Venture to Gnomeregan and kill Mekgineer Thermaplugg. Return to High Tinker Mekkatorque when the task is complete.\nMekgineer Thermaplugg slain","desc":"I trusted Thermaplugg, ‹race›. Never did I expect that he would betray me and the entire gnomish people. And for what? Power? Wealth? All things that he would have had in time. Now we have been displaced from our home and that madman is in charge. The king of nothing....\nWe will retake Gnomeregan, ‹name›. We will not stop until the city is back in our control. If you wish to join in our fight, a simple task I ask of you: Kill the betrayer. Destroy Mekgineer Thermaplugg.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCivinad Robes Triprunner Dungarees Dual Reinforced Leggings\nMoney: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,750\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Is the task complete? Did he beg for lenience? For mercy??","done":"I like to think that the last thing that went through his head as he collapsed to the ground was your foot, ‹race›. With Thermaplugg dead, our plans to retake Gnomeregan are one step closer to becoming a reality.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.1,"y":29,"n":"High Tinker Mekkatorque","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["gnomeregan"]},"529":{"id":529,"t":"Battle of Hillsbrad","lv":26,"min":19,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Blacksmith Verringtan and 4 Hillsbrad Apprentice Blacksmiths.\nRetrieve a shipment of iron and report back to Darthalia in Tarren Mill.\nShipment of Iron Shipment of Iron\nBlacksmith Verringtan slain\nHillsbrad Apprentice Blacksmith slain : 0/ 4","desc":"The humans of Hillsbrad have been putting up unexpected resistance. The problem appears to be that the townsfolk are being armed by the local blacksmith. We need to shut down all supply lines.\nYour mission will be to execute Blacksmith Verringtan. Slay his apprentices as well. While there, bring back a shipment of iron from their stockpile. The supplies will come in handy when we are done with the conquering of Hillsbrad and begin razing Southshore.","rew":"Money: 20 0 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,100\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Were you able to carry out your orders, ‹class›? Did you dispose of Verringtan and his assistants? And where is that iron shipment?","done":"Mission accomplished, ‹class›. And carried out quite skillfully, I might add.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.3,"y":20.5,"n":"High Executor Darthalia","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"689":{"id":689,"t":"A King's Tribute","lv":31,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Grand Mason Marblesten of Ironforge wants 5 pieces of Alterac Granite.\n5 Alterac Granite Alterac Granite","desc":"So our good King would like a memorial built in honor of a soldier named Sully Balloo? And you say the poor chap died during the Thandol Span tragedy?\nBah, will there ever be peace on Azeroth?\nNonetheless, any commission from the King is of utmost importance. To build a truly epic and lasting piece I want to work with one of the finest stones available. Travel to Darrow Hill in Hillsbrad and gather for me some Alterac Granite.","rew":"Experience: 2,500\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"‹name›, ‹name›, ‹name›! Tell me you have enough Alterac Granite for me to begin my masterpiece in honor of Sully Balloo.","done":"Perfect! Better than I could have imagined!\nAnd I have quite an imagination you know...\nDun Morogh Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":57.3,"y":35.2,"n":"Grand Mason Marblesten","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"7809":{"id":7809,"t":"A Donation of Mageweave","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Mageweave Cloth Northshire Guard 54.5 % , Deep Dweller 48.4 % , Refuge Pointe Defender 40.7 % , Stonard Hunter 40.2 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 3,300\n+150 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Mageweave is running low, and we could use your help to replenish our stocks! By counting on the community as a whole, we would only need a donation of 60 pieces of mageweave cloth from you to enable us to reach our goal. Such generosity would not go unnoticed by the Gnomeregan Exiles, I assure you!\nIf you have the sixty pieces of mageweave cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.","done":"Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63,"y":28.8,"n":"Bubulo Acerbus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"2849":{"id":2849,"t":"Wild Leather Vest","lv":45,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 2 Turtle Scale Breastplates, 2 Turtle Scale Gloves, and a Wildvine to Pratt McGrubben in Feathermoon Stronghold.\n2 Turtle Scale Breastplate\n2 Turtle Scale Gloves\nWildvine Retherokk the Berserker 80.6 % , Zul'arek Hatefowler 65.1 % , Purple Lotus 10 % , Vilebranch Aman'zasi Guard 9.5 % and 4 more","desc":"Wild Leather vests are the staple of any Wild Leather armor set. The frame of the vest blends with the wildvine to produce a product that offers maximum protection of the torso while allowing for the potent magic to work its way through the garment.\nFor this pattern, I will require two Turtle Scale breastplates, two sets of Turtle Scale gloves, and a wildvine. It's a tall order, but one you should have little difficulty in filling for me.","rew":"You will receive:\nPattern: Wild Leather Vest\nExperience: 2,900","back":"Do you have the two Turtle Scale breastplates and gloves I ordered? Also, don't forget the wildvine!\nEven with the earliest patterns, we learn that the fundamentals of shape translate well into more difficult garments. Though different items, the shape of the Turtle Scale breastplates prepares you for the detailing needed to make a Wild Leather vest.\nAnd the gloves... well, they're just for my own benefit. Remember, you're working for me!","done":"These are some very nice pieces here, ‹name›. The craftsmanship and care put in to making these alone would fetch several silver more than the average piece made.\nYou've filled my order, and with that comes your reward. The knowledge of making Wild Leather vests is now yours!","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":30.6,"y":42.7,"n":"Pratt McGrubben","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["leatherworking"]},"9089":{"id":9089,"t":"Dreamwalker Spaulders","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rayne at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Dreamwalker Spaulders if you bring her the following: 1 Desecrated Spaulders, 12 Wartorn Leather Scraps, 5 Cured Rugged Hides and 1 Nexus Crystal.\nDesecrated Spaulders Grobbulus 0 % in Naxxramas , Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Patchwerk 0 % in Naxxramas\n12 Wartorn Leather Scrap Skeletal Steed 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Necro Knight Guardian 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 24.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 24.1 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n5 Cured Rugged Hide\nNexus Crystal","desc":"Many heroes fell in the last war and many continue to perish at the hands of the Scourge to this day. From the corpses of the fallen, the armor is stripped and taken back to Naxxramas to be used for unknown purposes.\nRecover the desecrated armor and wartorn armor scraps and supply to me the other material components I require and I will craft Dreamwalker armor.","rew":"You will receive:\nDreamwalker Spaulders\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"The material cost is high, but soon forgotten.","done":"Your Dreamwalker Spaulders are ready, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.4,"y":49.3,"n":"Rayne","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"97249":{"id":97249,"t":"Favorite food","lv":15,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring Migi's Lunch to him behind Grommash Hold\nProvided: Migi's Lunch","desc":"Now that I know his parents worry about how much he's actually filling that belly, I've got an idea.\nThey made me promise not to pack the same meal every day, so Migi grows a taste for more than one thing. Still, whenever the smoker's full and we're making sweetglazed hog belly sandwiches, he always shows up for lunch. We've started crumbling the leftover crispy glazed bits as a topping--something we can add daily.\nTake this to him. Maybe he'll start showing up early and bringing friends!","back":"I think we can win this one...","done":"Borstan's Meats? Is that for one of us?\nOh!\nWow... this smells really good! Yummy.\nThanks for bringing me my lunch. I can tell what Borstan is going to be serving daily when my friends and I walk the road to Grommash Hold, by the smells alone. This tastes like my favorite, the sweetglaze! But it's different. I like the strong flavored crumbs.\nIf it's going to be this tasty every day, I think we need to stop our game to take our lunch together!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":57.4,"y":53.4,"n":"Borstan","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":36.8,"y":29,"n":"Migi","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"5729":{"id":5729,"t":"Hidden Enemies","lv":15,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Neeru Fireblade in Orgrimmar.","desc":"I think our next step should be to have you placed close to Neeru. If he is as agitated as reports suggest, then we may accomplish two things. One, you may be able to gain some greater knowledge about the Council or at least the Burning Blade, and two, he may just begin to trust you enough that he asks you to start to aid him. He may very well look at you as someone who can fill the void now that some of the leadership is in turmoil.\nReturn to the Cleft and speak to him again, but do not be too overt.","rew":"Experience: 110","done":"What is it?! Oh, you, ‹class›... my apologies. My anger rivals that of a rabid kodo bull... but perhaps it is my own fault. In sending travelers into Ragefire Chasm, I should have seen the possibility that some harm would come from it. It seems both Bazzalan and Jergosh were taken unaware and slain by some of Thrall's do-gooders. A most inopportune time, but there is nothing that can be done about it now.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.7,"y":37.8,"n":"Thrall","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":49.5,"y":50.6,"n":"Neeru Fireblade","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"9009":{"id":9009,"t":"Saving the Best for Last","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Mokvar your Devout Crown and Devout Robe.\nDevout Crown Darkmaster Gandling 0 %\nDevout Robe General Drakkisath 0 %","desc":"A truly amazing story, ‹name›! You have my thanks, and the heartfelt gratitude of all who were involved, I can assure you. Through your efforts we are delivered from the mistakes of our past.\nAs to your reward, I believe I have a few things that you have definitely earned and will truly enjoy.","rew":"You will receive:\nVirtuous Crown Virtuous Robe\nExperience: 1,650","back":"As per our deal, are you ready to hand over your Devout pieces in exchange for your new Virtuous Crown and Robe?","done":"I will truly miss you, ‹name›. There is a debt that I owe you, which I may never be able to repay.\nEnjoy your new head and chest armor. May it protect you for a long time to come, and help you to achieve even greater honor!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"1649":{"id":1649,"t":"The Tome of Valor","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind.","desc":"Valor, and all the virtues that go along with it, are like rare minerals: you must cherish them when you find them because of their value, but you must also take time to harvest them... refine them. When mixed together properly, a strong alloy is formed, sometimes unbreakable by even the most powerful blows.\nThis strength, your faith, your bravery, must be tested. You must learn to never lose faith and realize that with the power of the Light, you can overcome things that most others cannot.","rew":"Experience: 390","done":"Ah, you wish to petition me for a test of valor. Splendid.\nThere are many tasks throughout the city and surrounding lands that hold much challenge, and they could use a man/woman with your skills.\nThis test should not be taken lightly, ‹name›. This, like many things along our path, could take our lives. The Church always wishes to bolster its ranks, but it understands the sacrifices needed to ensure the paladins serving it are worthy.\nAre you prepared?","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50.5,"y":47.5,"n":"Duthorian Rall","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5649":{"id":5649,"t":"In Favor of Spirituality","lv":4,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Tai'jin in Durotar.","desc":"Aye, mon. Our kind have joined the Horde because they be good for us. They loyal, and they teach us much 'bout tings like honor. But our old ways die hard. The orcs may not approve of all our traditions, but that not mean we can't continue to practice some them in secret.\nYou know this, an' that's why I send you to Tai'jin in Razor Hill. She teach you more 'bout our history. She teach you the ways of our tribe. Go to her when you be ready.","rew":"Experience: 90","done":"Ahh... so you finally come to Tai'jin. This be good.\nYou already know that we are not da same tribe that once joined with the Horde. We be much stronger now. We stronger 'cause we adapt--the Horde teach us that much. We no longer defeat our enemies and gain strength from them; now we gain strength, and then defeat our enemies.\nThe difference be subtle, but you will learn. You will see. The tribe count on you to learn such things.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.4,"y":68.8,"n":"Ken'jai","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":54.3,"y":42.9,"n":"Tai'jin","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"129":{"id":129,"t":"A Free Lunch","lv":15,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Parker's lunch to Guard Parker. He patrols the road leading to Darkshire.\nParker's Lunch\nProvided: Parker's Lunch","desc":"Can you do me a favor? I've prepared a lunch for Guard Parker, but he's out on patrol...he's a big, strong Stormwind guard who can defend himself, but it's much too dangerous out there for a townsperson like me.\nSo if you deliver his lunch for me, then come back here and I'll give you a free lunch! Parker patrols the stretch of road leading to Duskwood.","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"Darcy sent me a lunch, did she? Such a kind heart she has. Well...let's have it!","done":"Thanks, I could really use the meal. Guarding Lakeshire from the orcs and gnolls is tough work!","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":21.5,"y":44.3,"n":"Darcy","s":1},{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":10.2,"y":71.5,"n":"Guard Parker","e":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"2609":{"id":2609,"t":"The Touch of Zanzil","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 1,150 experience instead of 1,200, 0.96 times as much.","obj":"Bring Doc Mixilpixil one bundle of Simple Wildflowers, one Leaded Vial, one Bronze Tube, and one Spool of Light Chartreuse Silk Thread. The 'itis' doesn't cure itself, young fella/lady.\nSimple Wildflowers sold by Bernard Gump , sold by Felicia Gump , sold by Nida Winterhoof\nLeaded Vial sold by Amy Davenport , sold by Antonio Perelli , sold by Dawn Brightstar , sold by Gunder Thornbush and 4 more\nBronze Tube Arcane Nullifier X-21 2.9 % , Mechanized Guardian 2 % , Mechano-Tank 2 % , XT:4 1.9 % and 4 more\nSpool of Light Chartreuse Silk Thread Spool of Light Chartreuse Silk Thread","desc":"It's unanimous, ‹name›. You've got the 'itis.'\nLuckily, I have a cure for the 'itis.'\nHere's what I need: One bundle of simple wildflowers, one leaded vial, one bronze tube, and last but certainly not least, one spool of light chartreuse silk thread. Ol' Emma left a spool of it for me at 'The Finest Thread.' You can find the shop along the canals.\nHurry along now, ‹name›, and try not to touch anyone until you're cured. Oh, and Dr. Montgomery says you need a shower -- his words, not mine.","rew":"You will receive:\nEau de Mixilpixil\nExperience: 1,150","back":"If you want the 'itis' cured, you're going to have to try harder than that, ‹name›. Where are the reagents for the cure?","done":"What am I doing? What does it look like I'm doing? I'm devising a cure for your 'itis!' Don't get indignant with me now, ‹name›!\nJust a few more seconds. There! Just spray this, um, fantastic smelling medicine on yourself and you'll be as good as new.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":80.1,"y":69.9,"n":"Doc Mixilpixil","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"4449":{"id":4449,"t":"Caught!","lv":45,"min":43,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 8 Dark Iron Geologists and bring 15 pieces of Silk Cloth to the person locked in the outhouse in Searing Gorge.\n15 Silk Cloth Protector Weaver , Mountaineer Langarr 85.7 % , Watcher Wollpert 85.7 % , Mountaineer Zwarn 78.3 % and 4 more\nDark Iron Geologist slain : 0/ 8","desc":"Hey! Hey, you! Get over here!\nYa gotta help me out. I was runnin' from them Dark Iron dwarves, and I hid in here to get out of sight. Damn bastard geologists and their magic ways! They musta seen me hide, cause next thing I knew, they locked the door and stuck me in here.\nTeach them geologists a lesson! Oh... an' can ya get me some pieces of silk cloth for... for... nothin'.","rew":"Experience: 3,900","back":"I ain't got all day! Get me those pieces of silk cloth! I mean geologists. Get those geologists! They deserve to feel my, well... your wrath.","done":"Oh, this is great! Nice feel to it too!\nWhat? Oh, yeah... geologists. Got 'em good, did ya? I can't thank ya enough, ‹name›. That'll give me some time to finish up in here... I mean, it'll let me not have to worry about them comin' back for me anytime soon. Thanks again.","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":65.6,"y":62.2,"n":"Wooden Outhouse","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"7729":{"id":7729,"t":"JOB OPPORTUNITY: Culling the Competition","lv":48,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay 15 Dark Iron Taskmasters and 15 Dark Iron Slavers. Return to Taskmaster Scrange in the Searing Gorge once you have accomplished this task.\nDark Iron Taskmaster slain : 0/ 15\nDark Iron Slaver slain : 0/ 15","desc":"Taskmaster Scrange is looking for a few good men and women to help 'cull the competition' in the Searing Gorge.\nIf you are interested in this position, venture out into the Searing Gorge and slaughter every Dark Iron Taskmaster and Dark Iron Slaver that you see.\nReturn to Taskmaster Scrange when your clothes are bloody enough.\nYou'll know when they're bloody enough so don't ask.","rew":"Money: 2 10 2 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Thorium Brotherhood","back":"We're gonna need to weigh you with and without clothes to be sure.","done":"15.9 pounds! That may be a new record for blood and gut weight on apparel! Congratulations, ‹class›!","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":37.6,"y":26.5,"n":"Wanted/Missing/Lost & Found","s":1},{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":39,"y":27.5,"n":"Taskmaster Scrange","e":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"8769":{"id":8769,"t":"A Ticking Present","lv":40,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nTicking Present","done":"Have a joyous Feast of Great-Winter from your friends at Smokeywood Pastures.\nOrgrimmar Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":52.3,"y":69.3,"n":"Ticking Present","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.5,"y":31.8,"n":"Ticking Present","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"3089":{"id":3089,"t":"Rune-Inscribed Parchment","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Rune-Inscribed Parchment and speak to Shikrik in the Valley of Trials.\nRune-Inscribed Parchment\nProvided: Rune-Inscribed Parchment","desc":"Ah, while you were gone a parchment came for you, ‹name›.\nRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the shaman trainer Shikrik. She would have words with you when you're ready.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"So, you've arrived. I was beginning to wonder when you would show yourself. I sent the parchment some time ago--I wasn't sure if it had arrived.\nBut enough chatter... you're here because you have been chosen, chosen to lead the spiritual lives of our people.","done":"You will be the conduit in which our ancestors communicate. You will have the power of the elements at your beck and call. Sundering your enemies will be child's play; healing your allies as easy as breathing. Keep these things in mind as you face new challenges, and come back to me as often as you'd like. I will remain here to teach you new spells and set you on the correct path when you are ready.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.1,"y":68.3,"n":"Gornek","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":42.4,"y":69,"n":"Shikrik","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"94449":{"id":94449,"t":"Call of fire","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find Bruegs Kindleborn in Dun Morogh.","desc":"It's been long since ye were last tested, ‹name›. Ye've shown patience, aye -- but now it's time ye learned of chaos... of destruction. Fire's call is loud, and if ye're ready to pay its price, it'll speak to ye.\nSeek out Bruegs Kindleborn, far east in the mountains. He dwells in a cave above South Gate Outpost. He'll know if ye're truly ready.","done":"Hmm... that elder sent ye, eh? Well, a ‹class›'s word is solid, so I'll not argue. That means ye're ready for the next sapta. The sapta of fire. I see it in yer eyes already -- the burnin', the hunger. Ye've tasted power, and now ye want more. But mind yerself, Shamfor. Remember what the stone taught ye. Fire's easy to wield, but harder to master. Know when to hold back.\nDun Morogh Ironforge","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":47.4,"y":52,"n":"Ingrid Dunwald","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":87.6,"y":43.6,"n":"Bruegs Kindleborn","e":1},{"z":"Ironforge","x":47.4,"y":13.6,"n":"Eldrun Stormbreaker","s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"449":{"id":449,"t":"The Deathstalkers' Report","lv":11,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Deathstalker Report to High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher.\nDeathstalker Report\nProvided: Deathstalker Report","desc":"Although Quinn's wounds are mending, I want to get our report to High Executor Hadrec as quickly as possible. It has information that is vital to the Forsaken's occupation of Silverpine.","rew":"Money: 2 0 gold, 2 silver, 0 copper Experience: 440\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"Did you discover the fate of the Deathstalkers?","done":"I hadn't accounted for the level of Scourge presence we've seen in Silverpine Forest, nor for the troubles our Deathstalkers have had in their scouting efforts.\nYour aid to our Deathstalkers was invaluable, ‹name›. And you will be commended.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":53.5,"y":13.4,"n":"Rane Yorick","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":43.4,"y":40.9,"n":"High Executor Hadrec","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"1089":{"id":1089,"t":"The Den","lv":29,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to the Den on Stonetalon Peak. Using the Gatekeeper's Key, obtain the druids' hidden items. Use these items to open the Talon Den Hoard.\nSleepers' Key Sleepers' Cache\nClaw Key Druids' Cache\nBarrow Key Barrow Cache","desc":"The druids built the Talon Den on Stonetalon Peak, where they keep many powerful items.\nThey devised a complex scheme to keep them from falling into the wrong hands.\nLuckily, I managed to... extract some details from one of them.\nHidden in a small lantern at the entrance of the Den, you will find the Gatekeeper's Key--with it you will be able to open caches around the Den. The items from these caches will allow you to open their hoard, located in one of the central areas.","rew":"You will receive:\nSacred Band Panther Armor Juggernaut Leggings\nExperience: 2,950","back":"Three keyholes are carved into the stone.","done":"As the three keys are slid into their matching openings, in the middle of the glowing light a number of items appear.","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":45.9,"y":60.4,"n":"Braelyn Firehand","s":1},{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":26.6,"y":10.9,"n":"Talon Den Hoard","e":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"1249":{"id":1249,"t":"The Missing Diplomat","lv":33,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Subdue Tapoke Jahn before he escapes, and then return to Mikhail in Menethil.","desc":"You say Elling sent you here? Well then, the hospitality I expressed is now tenfold. Anything you need, just ask. I will do my best to aid you.\nHmm, Slim, you say? Not sure the name sounds familiar, but I'll keep my eyes out for him.\nDon't look now, ‹name›, but the gentleman over by the exit is looking over here. He's listening to our conversation a little too intently if you catch my meaning? If I were you, I'd do what you can to subdue him before he makes a break for the door.","rew":"Experience: 1,300\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Did he slip away? He looked a little shady the way he was watching us.","done":"Caught him, huh? Good for you. I'm surprised that was Slim.\nI'll be honest, I never thought I'd miss the excitement of some of the more devious underground activities. I guess old habits die hard. Don't mention that to Elling--he'd probably try and get me to come back to Stormwind if he heard I missed the action.\nI'm glad I could at least be of a little service to you while you were in Menethil. If you need anything else, just ask.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":10.6,"y":60.8,"n":"Mikhail","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"97329":{"id":97329,"t":"Wheres the key","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Primitive Key obtained from the trolls at the Ruins of Zul'kunda in Stranglethorn Vale to Zimmix Sputterspark.\nPrimitive Key","desc":"You! Yes, you! Come here, keep your voice down!\nI screwed up big time. I managed to secure a sweet deal for Booty Bay to use their zeppelin tower for expedited deliveries and on our very first route I saw a huge bird--err, got SHOT DOWN just to the east of here!\nI survived the crash, unfortunately, but before I woke up, I was already being dragged by my ears! Now I'm surrounded by bloodthirsty trolls and locked in a cage!\nLook, I just need the key, okay? I can escape on my own.","rew":"Money: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,750\nLevel 35 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 31 33 38 44 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 97329\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 35, 5,500 XP in all.\n1 [ 35 ] Where's the Key? this quest\nBring the Primitive Key obtained from the trolls at the Ruins of Zul'kunda in Stranglethorn Vale to Zimmix Sputterspark.\n2,750 XP\n2 [ 35 ] Zimmix's Great Escape\nEscort Zimmix Sputterspark away from the Ruins of Zul'Kunda then tell Wharfmaster Lozgil in Booty Bay of your successful rescue.\n2,750 XP","cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"209":{"id":209,"t":"Skullsplitter Tusks","lv":42,"min":37,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Acquire 18 Skullsplitter Tusks and return them to Kebok.\n18 Skullsplitter Tusk Ana'thek the Cruel 21 % , Skullsplitter Beastmaster 21 % , Skullsplitter Berserker 21 % , Skullsplitter Scout 21 % and 4 more","desc":"It's expensive and hard to kill enough tigers to support the export of tiger fangs to the islands in the South Seas. Luckily, we've developed a technique that allows us to take mundane horn-like objects and turn them into undetectable forgeries.\nThe closest match we've found, amazingly, are the tusks of the Skullsplitter trolls.\nHey, before you say anything, what the buyer doesn't know doesn't hurt them, am I right? Bring me a large number of them so we can get to work on the monthly shipment!","rew":"Money: 55 0 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,450\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Tough buggers, aren't they? Well, have you had any luck? Sorry to seem impatient, but this has been a huge thorn in my side! Well?","done":"Ah, good work, good work! Ugh, though you could have done a better job cleaning off the-- Well, no matter, no matter! My thanks to you, ‹name›, our operation will no doubt see increased output and productivity thanks to your help! Good good, now, onto other matters...","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27,"y":77.1,"n":"Kebok","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"609":{"id":609,"t":"Voodoo Dues","lv":44,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Maury's Clubbed Foot, Jon-Jon's Golden Spyglass, and Chucky's Huge Ring to \"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley in Booty Bay.\nMaury's Clubbed Foot Maury \"Club Foot\" Wilkins\nJon-Jon's Golden Spyglass Jon-Jon the Crow\nChucky's Huge Ring Chucky \"Ten Thumbs\"","desc":"My list is shortening, but there are still people who owe me.\nNext, we have Maury \"Club Foot\" Wilkins, Jon-Jon the Crow, and Chucky \"Ten Thumbs.\"\nThese scurvy dogs' debts are months outstanding and I thought they skipped town to avoid paying up! Later, I heard they're cursed and bewitched and now wander the jungle ruins. But I don't care what their fate is - I want what's mine!\nThey're at the Ruins of Aboraz and the Ruins of Jubuwal, northeast of here. Find them, and collect.","rew":"Money: 65 0 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,750\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"‹name›, did you find those three dogs? Did you collect their valuables?","done":"Great! I can get a good price for these, especially for what's inside Maury's foot! Thanks much, ‹name›!\nI hope those three learned their lesson: don't bet something you can't afford to lose.\nAnd maybe it's too late for them, but...they should be careful of who they gamble with.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.8,"y":77.1,"n":"\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"929":{"id":929,"t":"Crown of the Earth","lv":5,"min":3,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Fill the Jade Phial and bring it back to Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar.\nFilled Jade Phial\nProvided: Jade Phial","desc":"First, let me tell you more of the task you must complete. The druids in Darnassus use the water of the moonwells of Teldrassil, and their moonwell must be replenished from time to time. Using these specially crafted phials, you can collect the water of the moonwells.\nTake this vessel to the moonwell outside of Starbreeze Village to the east, and fill it with some of its waters, then return to me. When you have completed your task, I shall continue the story where Tenaron left off...","rew":"Experience: 340\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Hello again, ‹name›. Have you completed your task?","done":"After the Battle of Mount Hyjal, we were without direction. Nordrassil smoked from the fire it unleashed, and our immortality--the very essence of our beings!--was lost.\nIt was in this trying time that the Betrayer was freed from his prison, and Shan'do Stormrage disappeared. A dark time for all.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.1,"y":61.7,"n":"Corithras Moonrage","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"849":{"id":849,"t":"Revenge of Gann","lv":26,"min":17,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Destroy the flying machine at Bael Modan and return to Gann Stonespire.\nBael Modan Flying Machine destroyed\nProvided: Explosive Stick of Gann","desc":"Following Khazgorm's plans it should be no problem to fashion an explosive charge\nAh, there we go.\nNow, ‹name›, I am going to entrust you with a special task. Take this explosive stick and use it to blow up the flying machine at Bael Modan.\nNot only is the flying machine a key part of the site's infrastructure it also serves as a weapon of war. More importantly it is an icon of power and an insult to the memory of my tribe.\nMake me proud by completing this heroic task and you shall be rewarded.","rew":"You will receive:\nTotemic Clan Ring\nMoney: 20 0 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,100\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Once the dwarven flying machine has been destroyed I will feel the sweet satisfaction of revenge.","done":"You have done well, ‹name›! May you be revered in Thunder Bluff as a defender of sacred tauren lands and a champion of the lost tribe.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":45.9,"y":77,"n":"Gann Stonespire","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"2769":{"id":2769,"t":"The Brassbolts Brothers","lv":46,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Wizzle Brassbolts in the Shimmering Flats.","desc":"Have you met the Brassbolts brothers? They're over in the Shimmering Flats, in Kalimdor, racing their rocket car against the goblins. They usually win which is no surprise--the goblin car blows up so much it barely ever crosses the finish line!\nBut even then, the Brassbolts brothers are always looking for new ways to make their car go faster, and Wizzle told me he needs a very rare component for his next experiment.\nHe probably needs help getting that part. Speak to him and find out.","rew":"Experience: 410","done":"Ah, you want to help me? Great!\nThere's a part I want for an experiment I'm working on, and I need a brave ‹class› like you to help me get it!\nDun Morogh Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62,"y":28.5,"n":"Klockmort Spannerspan","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":78.1,"y":77.1,"n":"Wizzle Brassbolts","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"769":{"id":769,"t":"Kodo Hide Bag","lv":10,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 4 Light Leather and 4 Coarse Thread to Veren Tallstrider in Thunder Bluff.\n4 Light Leather Tattered Chest 18 % , Battered Chest 18 % , Armor Crate 0 % , Tattered Chest 0 % and 4 more\n4 Coarse Thread sold by Tharynn Bouden , sold by Amy Davenport , sold by Gina MacGregor , sold by Gunder Thornbush and 4 more","desc":"The kodo beasts of Mulgore are strong and sturdy -- traits much respected among us. If you are skilled in leatherworking and wish the knowledge to make a Kodo Hide Bag, then bring me supplies for my trade.\nDo this, and I will share my knowledge with you.","rew":"You will receive:\nPattern: Kodo Hide Bag\nExperience: 420\n+50 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Do you have my supplies, ‹name›?","done":"Ah, good. Thank you, ‹name›. My heart swells with pride to see youths interested in the craft of leatherworking.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":44.4,"y":44.7,"n":"Veren Tallstrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"369":{"id":369,"t":"A New Plague","lv":11,"min":6,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Apothecary Johaan in the town of Brill wants you to bring him 4 samples of venom from a Vicious Night Web Spider.\n4 Vicious Night Web Spider Venom Vicious Night Web Spider 50 %","desc":"While you were out gathering, I uncovered some old text in one of my tomes that indicates that an ancient plague wiped out thousands of innocent victims. Later it was discovered that the deadly agent in the plague was preserved through the venom of Night Web Spiders.\nBring me some venom from a Vicious Night Web Spider to complete this experiment. I want to see if the contagious element from the venom will work with my new concoction. Rumor has it the spiders can be found in Eastern Tirisfal Glades.","rew":"You will receive:\nApprentice Sash\nExperience: 220\n+25 reputation with Undercity","back":"Do you have some venom from a Vicious Night Web Spider yet, ‹name›? It's the final component I need in order to test my experiment.","done":"Ah, this venom will do perfectly, ‹name›. Everything else has been added to my concoction and boiled down. Finally, I am ready to try this new deadly agent!","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":59.4,"y":52.4,"n":"Apothecary Johaan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"4289":{"id":4289,"t":"The Apes of Un'Goro","lv":55,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 2 Un'Goro Gorilla Pelts, 2 Un'Goro Stomper Pelts, and 2 Un'Goro Thunderer Pelts to Torwa Pathfinder at the entrance of Un'Goro Crater.\n2 Un'Goro Gorilla Pelt Un'Goro Gorilla\n2 Un'Goro Stomper Pelt Un'Goro Stomper\n2 Un'Goro Thunderer Pelt Un'Goro Thunderer","desc":"This crater has many strange creatures--they seem to be nobler versions of the creatures found throughout my homeland and beyond. I cannot explain it, but this place cries of the Earth Mother. I pay homage to her every time I track one of her beautiful creatures across its basin.\nIf you too wish to feel the enlightenment that accompanies such a great feat, then head to the north. There you'll find great apes who are a test for any mortal's strength. Bring me their pelts... prove your strength.","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,650","back":"Have the creatures here bested you already, ‹name›?\nDo not be dissuaded so easily. Tracking and defeating the apes of Un'Goro is no simple task, even for a great hunter.","done":"So, you have proven strong, strong enough to best the great apes of Un'Goro--that is good. The challenge was small compared to Lar'korwi, but I will not take such a great victory away from you.\nThese pelts will make wonderful clothing for my tribe. You have helped me and proven worthy.\nBefore you set off on another task, let us give praise to the Earth Mother and thank the spirits of those apes you killed--they must know their deaths will not be wasted.","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":71.6,"y":76,"n":"Torwa Pathfinder","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"3569":{"id":3569,"t":"Seeping Corruption","lv":52,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Cuely's Elixir to Thersa Windsong in Undercity.\nCuely's Elixir\nProvided: Cuely's Elixir","desc":"Give this to Thersa. Perhaps it will cure her... perhaps not. We really won't know until after she drinks it.","rew":"Experience: 500","back":"I've come to Undercity because I heard their alchemists have been studying long and hard on how to find a cure for their own illness. It was suggested that perhaps they could help me too.\nAlthough this place makes me feel far from welcome, I had no choice--the sickness that found me is tearing me up inside and I needed their help immediately.","done":"Chemist Cuely has been very accommodating... disturbingly so. But if he says this will help me, then I have no other choice. I don't have time to find any other solution. I've already spoken to priests and shamans, none of which could help me.\nLet us hope that the Earthmother watches over my spirit.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":48.7,"y":71.4,"n":"Chemist Cuely","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":49,"y":70.8,"n":"Thersa Windsong","e":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"1489":{"id":1489,"t":"Hamuul Runetotem","lv":16,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 10 instead of 12. Partly read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Speak with Hamuul Runetotem.","desc":"The shells you brought me have a taint, one I have never before seen. I am certain the water of the Oases is the cause, and I can sense the confusion they cause this land. It is as if the land dreams and cannot awake.\nThe Wailing Caverns must be the source of the taint. But before you go there, speak with Hamuul Runetotem, the elder druid. I sent word to him of the happenings in the Barrens. He is wise, and can offer you counsel.\nYou will find him in Thunder Bluff, on the Elder Rise.","rew":"Experience: 290\n+25 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"I bid you greetings, ‹name›. You are welcome here, and I suggest you gather all your strength. For the task we now set before you ... is a dire one.\nThe Barrens Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.3,"y":31.9,"n":"Tonga Runetotem","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":78.6,"y":28.6,"n":"Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem","e":1}],"cats":["wailing-caverns"]},"49":{"id":49,"t":"Sweet Amber","lv":44,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Grimbooze Thunderbrew wants a Sack of Barley, a Sack of Rye and a Sack of Corn.\nSack of Barley Sack of Barley\nSack of Corn Sack of Corn\nSack of Rye Sack of Rye","desc":"Amber is the hue of my life's longest love\nLike the last embers of dusk in the sky above\nRetrieve for me so that my love shall be born\nOne sack of each: barley, rye and corn.","rew":"Money: 1 25 1 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,650","back":"Encore? Well, sure!\nAmber is the hue of my life's longest love\nLike the last embers of dusk in the sky above\nRetrieve for me so that my love shall be born\nOne sack of each: barley, rye and corn.","done":"Hiccup! Ho ho!\nWestfall Swamp of Sorrows Tanaris The Hinterlands","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":44.6,"y":80.3,"n":"Grimbooze Thunderbrew","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"98209":{"id":98209,"t":"Bloom of the heavens","lv":29,"min":22,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring Nord'el to Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine in Darkshore.\nYou recall Sylessa mentioning a boat in Menethil Harbor can take you there.\nProvided: Nord'el","desc":"Would you please deliver Nord'el to elder Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine?\nThe boat from here should be able to get you there swiftly.\nI apologize for the request, I truly do. I remain fatigued from my journey here--and from fleeing those murloc devils when I first attempted to retrieve the sacred bloom!","rew":"Money: 13 0 gold, 13 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,200\n+50 reputation with Darnassus\nWetlands Darkshore","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":8,"y":55.8,"n":"Sylessa Duskwhisper","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.4,"y":40.2,"n":"Thundris Windweaver","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"289":{"id":289,"t":"The Cursed Crew","lv":29,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 13 Cursed Sailors, 5 Cursed Marines and First Mate Snellig. Bring Snellig's Snuffbox to First Mate Fitzsimmons in Menethil Harbor.\nSnellig's Snuffbox First Mate Snellig\nCursed Sailor slain : 0/ 13\nCursed Marine slain : 0/ 5","desc":"<Bolstered, Fitzsimmons continues his tale...>\nI am the sole survivor of the ill-fated Third Fleet of Kul Tiras, wrecked off the coast to the north. But although I'm the only member of the fleet still breathing, I'm not the only one still walking about! For on one of our ships was hidden a great, and terrible treasure, and the eerie power of it keeps the souls of my brothers trapped within the ships' rotting hulls.\nBut if you can free some of my brothers, then perhaps you can break their curse.","rew":"Money: 19 0 gold, 19 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,750\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"In my dreams, I can sometimes hear the doomed moans of my brethren! Please, good sir, free them from the bonds and quiet their cries.","done":"My thanks to you, ‹name›. And the gratitude of my cursed brethren goes to you as well.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":10.9,"y":59.6,"n":"First Mate Fitzsimmons","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"92529":{"id":92529,"t":"Falaath village","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Report to Missionary Jasaan near the entrance to Falaath Village.\nIf you lose your Mark of Akir, speak with Sania Silverstream in Shen'dar Village to regain the effect.\nSpeak with Missionary Jasaan at the entrance to Falaath Village","desc":"It gladdens my heart that you wish to serve Al'Akir. Our current trials as a people stem from our own complacency. We grew prideful and took the bounty of the winds for granted. The stagnation that followed is the reason the spirits of the wind abandoned us.\nOnly through acts of contrition may we feel the wind's caress once more. If you seek the fellowship of like-minded shen'dorei, go to Falaath Village and find Missionary Jasaan there. I will mark you so that the faithful will know you as a recruit.","done":"What is this? A new acolyte seeking to serve the windlord sent by sister Sania? Truly we are blessed by the touch of the four winds this day!\nWe welcome all who seek to bask in the blessings of Al'Akir.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":44.8,"y":45.4,"n":"Sania Silverstream","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":46.8,"y":56.2,"n":"Missionary Jasaan","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"92849":{"id":92849,"t":"The missing scholar","lv":10,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Keep searching for Fillion Flamebreeze.\nFind Fillion Flamebreeze\nCarry Fillion Flamebreeze to safety while avoiding enemies","desc":"<Judging by what you've just found, its very likely that Fillion befell some misfortune here. He may still be nearby, and he might be in need of aid. You notice a cave just to the north of your current location. You should continue searching for him there.>","done":"Th... thank you, stranger. I was walking down the road on my way back to Valanaar when a looming shadow appeared overhead. I turned to look and saw a massive, terrible beast bearing down at me from the sky. I tried to run, but I was hit hard and the world went black.\nI think its fair to say that if you hadn't come along, I'd have been dinner for that beast and its young.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":53.3,"y":72.2,"n":"Bloodstained Satchel","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":52,"y":69.4,"n":"Fillion Flamebreeze","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"94369":{"id":94369,"t":"The fate of zephras","lv":12,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.\nSpeak with Talaanis Shadowsong","desc":"Ansirem has told me much of the elemental lords and I am afraid that we have good reason to fear Al'Akir now that the wards that have hidden Zephras are down. If the Windlord chooses to attack us, we stand no chance to defend ourselves while we are here in his domain.\nHigh Elder Shadowsong needs to know of the danger we are in, and more importantly, what our intentions are for our mission to Azeroth. We will find the means to save our home. I swear it.","done":"<Talaanis Shadowsong listens intently as you tell him of what transpired above the Shrine of Akir, and of Elaadrin's plan to leave Zephras Isle.>\nI need to reflect on this further, but looking at the upside, we have rid ourselves of Lorthuna and deprived the cult of their leader. Our home has not been invaded yet, and on the timeline of elemental demigods, it could be years... decades even, before Al'Akir deigns to turn his attention to us.\nThere is much to fear now, but much to celebrate as well.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.6,"y":79.8,"n":"Elaadrin Evengale","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":76.6,"n":"Talaanis Shadowsong","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"93089":{"id":93089,"t":"What comes next","lv":13,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Elaadrin Evengale when you are prepared to leave Zephras Isle.","desc":"Please extend my thanks to Elaadrin for all that the High Order and your new friends from this \"Kirin Tor\" have done for Zephras Isle. I'm aware of the High Order's plans to leave the island, and your order has my blessing and well-wishes in this expedition.\nI can only hope that whatever arcane solution the High Order finds can truly provide us with the stability we've lacked these past years. If you plan to go with them... well, his mission will be all the stronger for it.\nWinds be with you, ‹name›.","done":"It gladdens me to hear that we have High Elder Shadowsong's blessing for our expedition. Now that the cult has been defeated and preparations have been made, I think it's finally time.\nAnsirem has worked diligently to help us get stable skycutter transport going between the city of Dalaran and Zephras Isle. We've done as much testing as we can, and the time has come for vanguard to depart.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":76.6,"n":"Talaanis Shadowsong","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.6,"y":79.8,"n":"Elaadrin Evengale","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"8049":{"id":8049,"t":"The Eye of Zuldazar","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","rew":"You will receive:\nThe Eye of Zuldazar\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","done":"Accept this talisman as a token of our appreciation, ‹class›.\nThe Eye of Zuldazar will grow in power as your bond with the trolls of Zandalar strengthens. Return to me periodically and I shall imbue the jewel.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16.1,"n":"Al'tabim the All-Seeing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});